":111},{"base":"H2063","lemma":"זֹאת","tr":"zot","gloss":"this","lang":"h","inPassage":4,"uses":604},{"base":"H5883","lemma":"עֵין רֹגֵל","tr":"en ro·gel","gloss":"En-rogel","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H0290","lemma":"אֲחִימַ֫עַץ","tr":"a·chi·ma·ats","gloss":"Ahimaaz","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":15}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"2SA","chapter":15,"verse":28,"verseEnd":28,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"See, I will wait at the fords of the wilderness until word comes from you to inform me.”","from":16},{"book":"2SA","chapter":15,"verse":36,"verseEnd":36,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"Indeed, their two sons, Ahimaaz son of Zadok and Jonathan son of Abiathar, are there with them. Send them to me with everything you hear.”","from":17},{"book":"JOS","chapter":15,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then the border went up to Debir from the Valley of Achor, turning north to Gilgal, which faces the Ascent of Adummim south of the ravine. It continued along the waters of En-shemesh and came out at En-rogel.","from":17},{"book":"JOS","chapter":18,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Then it went down to the foot of the hill that faces the Valley of Hinnom at the northern end of the Valley of Rephaim and ran down the Valley of Hinnom toward the southern slope of the Jebusites and downward to En-rogel.","from":17},{"book":"2SA","chapter":3,"verse":16,"verseEnd":16,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"Her husband followed her, weeping all the way to Bahurim. Then Abner said to him, “Go back.” So he returned home.","from":18},{"book":"2SA","chapter":15,"verse":27,"verseEnd":27,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"The king also said to Zadok the priest, “Are you not a seer? Return to the city in peace—you with your son Ahimaaz, and Abiathar with his son Jonathan.","from":17},{"book":"EXO","chapter":1,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The midwives answered Pharaoh, “The Hebrew women are not like the Egyptian women, for they are vigorous and give birth before a midwife arrives.”","from":19},{"book":"EXO","chapter":1,"verse":19,"verseEnd":19,"votes":0,"source":"tsk","text":"The midwives answered Pharaoh, “The Hebrew women are not like the Egyptian women, for they are vigorous and give birth before a midwife arrives.”","from":20}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":6}]},"23-29":{"people":[{"id":"ahithophel-h0302","name":"Ahithophel","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":23},{"id":"absalom-h0053","name":"Absalom","kind":"person","brief":"David's son","count":3,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"david-h1732","name":"David","kind":"person","brief":"King of Judah","count":3,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"israel-h3478","name":"Israel","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Isaac","count":2,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"abigail-h0026h","name":"Abigail","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of David","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"amasa-h6021g","name":"Amasa","kind":"person","brief":"An Ishmaelite","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"ishmael-h3458g","name":"Ishmael","kind":"person","brief":"Son of Abraham","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"jether-h3500h","name":"Jether","kind":"person","brief":"An Ishmaelite","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"joab-h3097g","name":"Joab","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"nahash-h5176i","name":"Nahash","kind":"person","brief":"Mother of David","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"zeruiah-h6870g","name":"Zeruiah","kind":"person","brief":"Sister of David","count":1,"firstVerse":25},{"id":"ammiel-h5988h","name":"Ammiel","kind":"person","brief":"Father of Machir","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"barzillai-h1271g","name":"Barzillai","kind":"person","brief":"David's compatriot","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"machir-h4353h","name":"Machir","kind":"person","brief":"Saul's family","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"nahash-h5176j","name":"Nahash","kind":"person","brief":"Ammonite king","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"shobi-h7629","name":"Shobi","kind":"person","brief":"An Ammonite","count":1,"firstVerse":27}],"places":[{"id":"mahanaim-h4266","name":"Mahanaim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":2,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"jordan-h3383","name":"Jordan","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":24},{"id":"gilead-h1568g","name":"Gilead","kind":"place","brief":"In Manasseh","count":2,"firstVerse":26},{"id":"ammon-h5983","name":"Ammon","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"lo-debar-h3810","name":"Lo-debar","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27},{"id":"rogelim-h7274","name":"Rogelim","kind":"place","brief":"","count":1,"firstVerse":27}],"words":[{"base":"H0053","lemma":"אֲבִישָׁלוֹם","tr":"a·vi·sha·lom","gloss":"Absalom","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":111},{"base":"H7039","lemma":"קָלִי","tr":"qa·li","gloss":"roasted","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":6},{"base":"H3810","lemma":"לֹא דְבָר","tr":"lo de·var","gloss":"Lo-debar","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":8},{"base":"H5176","lemma":"נָחָשׁ","tr":"na·chash","gloss":"Nahash","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":10},{"base":"H4266","lemma":"מַחֲנַיִם","tr":"ma·cha·na·yim","gloss":"Mahanaim","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":13},{"base":"H6021","lemma":"עֲמָשָׂא","tr":"a·ma·sa","gloss":"Amasa","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":16},{"base":"H1732","lemma":"דָּוִד","tr":"da·vid","gloss":"David","lang":"h","inPassage":3,"uses":1075},{"base":"H3097","lemma":"יוֹאָב","tr":"yo·av","gloss":"Joab","lang":"h","inPassage":2,"uses":145},{"base":"H2614","lemma":"חָנַק","tr":"cha·naq","gloss":"to strangle","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2},{"base":"H6321","lemma":"פּוֹל","tr":"pol","gloss":"bean","lang":"h","inPassage":1,"uses":2}],"parallels":[],"crossrefs":[{"book":"MAT","chapter":27,"verse":5,"verseEnd":5,"votes":9,"source":"both","text":"So Judas threw the silver into the temple and left. Then he went away and hanged himself.","from":23},{"book":"2SA","chapter":15,"verse":12,"verseEnd":12,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"While Absalom was offering the sacrifices, he sent for Ahithophel the Gilonite, Davidʼs counselor, to come from his hometown of Giloh. So the conspiracy gained strength, and Absalomʼs following kept increasing.","from":23},{"book":"2KI","chapter":20,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":7,"source":"both","text":"In those days Hezekiah became mortally ill. The prophet Isaiah son of Amoz came to him and said, “This is what the LORD says: ‘Put your house in order, for you are about to die; you will not recover.’”","from":23},{"book":"1KI","chapter":2,"verse":7,"verseEnd":7,"votes":6,"source":"both","text":"But show loving devotion to the sons of Barzillai the Gileadite, and let them be among those who eat at your table, because they stood by me when I fled from your brother Absalom.","from":27},{"book":"2SA","chapter":9,"verse":4,"verseEnd":4,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"“Where is he?” replied the king. And Ziba said, “Indeed, he is in Lo-debar at the house of Machir son of Ammiel.”","from":27},{"book":"2SA","chapter":10,"verse":1,"verseEnd":1,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"Some time later, the king of the Ammonites died and was succeeded by his son Hanun.","from":27},{"book":"2SA","chapter":10,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"openbible","text":"And David said, “I will show kindness to Hanun son of Nahash, just as his father showed kindness to me.” So David sent some of his servants to console Hanun concerning his father. But when they arrived in the land of the Ammonites,","from":27},{"book":"2SA","chapter":16,"verse":2,"verseEnd":2,"votes":5,"source":"both","text":"“Why do you have these?” asked the king. Ziba replied, “The donkeys are for the kingʼs household to ride, the bread and summer fruit are for the young men to eat, and the wine is to refresh those who become exhausted in the wilderness.”","from":29}],"notes":[],"groups":[{"id":"kings-prophets","title":"Kings, prophets and the house of David","people":4},{"id":"patriarchs","title":"The patriarchal families","people":2}]}}